        <tr><td><strong>Dispensaries in Town</strong></td><td>2 (Full Bloom Cannabis, Royal Leaf Apothecary)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Nearby Dispensary</strong></td><td>Richardson Remedies — Bog Road, Caribou (~10 mi S, medical-only)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Population</strong></td><td>~8,700 (2020 Census)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>County</strong></td><td>Aroostook County (largest U.S. county east of the Mississippi)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>County Population</strong></td><td>~67,000 across 6,672 sq mi</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Dispensaries in Presque Isle</h2>

    <h3>Full Bloom Cannabis</h3>
    <p><strong>Address:</strong> 445 Main St, Presque Isle, ME 04769 (per fullbloomcannabis.com)<br>
    <strong>Phone:</strong> (207) 760-7586 (per fullbloomcannabis.com)<br>
    <strong>Hours:</strong> Mon–Thu 8am–9pm, Fri–Sat 8am–10pm, Sun 9am–7pm (per fullbloomcannabis.com)<br>
    <strong>Type:</strong> Adult-Use/Recreational — the operator's site labels both the Presque Isle and Grand Isle stores "Adult-Use/Recreational." Verify directly with the operator for medical-menu availability.</p>
    <p>Full Bloom Cannabis anchors Presque Isle's Main Street dispensary scene. Per the operator's site, "From Aroostook County, all the way down to York County, Full Bloom Cannabis products can be found on Adult-Use and recreational dispensary shelves." The Presque Isle store is one of two operator locations; Full Bloom also operates a Grand Isle location and cultivates its own flower. The Presque Isle store's location in the city's retail core makes it a natural stop for residents of Presque Isle, Fort Fairfield, Mars Hill, and the surrounding Aroostook communities.</p>

    <h3>Royal Leaf Apothecary</h3>
    <p><strong>Address:</strong> 415 Main St, Presque Isle, ME 04769 (per royalleafpot.com)<br>
    <strong>Phone:</strong> (207) 561-7667 (per royalleafpot.com and Yelp)<br>
    <strong>Hours:</strong> Open 365 days, 7:00am–10:00pm (per royalleafpot.com)<br>
    <strong>Type:</strong> <strong>Adult-Use only</strong> — the operator's site header states "Adult-Use Cannabis Dispensary." Royal Leaf's homepage links to an OCP advisory on medical-cannabis contamination rather than carrying medical product. Verify directly with the operator if you need a medical menu.</p>
    <p>Royal Leaf Apothecary operates the second of Presque Isle's two Main Street dispensaries. The store is positioned as an adult-use dispensary with a small-batch product focus and a consultation-style sales floor. Together with Full Bloom, Royal Leaf gives the city two full-service options within a few blocks of one another.</p>

    <h3>Richardson Remedies — Caribou (10 mi south)</h3>
    <p><strong>Address:</strong> Bog Road (no house number publicly listed), Caribou, ME 04736 (per The County, Sept 2024)<br>
    <strong>Type:</strong> Medical-only — Caribou voted to ban adult-use retail in September 2024 (per The County), so Richardson's Remedies is medical-only.</p>
    <p>For Presque Isle patients living south of the city, Richardson Remedies in Caribou is a 10-minute drive down US-1. The dispensary is a long-standing Aroostook operator (also listed in Caribou alongside Safe Alternatives on the Presque Isle Road) and gives the southern end of the county an additional medical-cannabis option beyond Presque Isle's two stores.</p>
  </section>

  <Callout title="March 2026 Moratorium (verified: The County + WAGM-TV)" type="insight">
    The Presque Isle City Council voted unanimously on March 4, 2026 to impose a temporary moratorium halting new adult-use and medical marijuana business applications while the city reviews its cannabis <a href="/guides/maine-cannabis-zoning-requirements">zoning</a>, density limits, and public-safety provisions. <a href="https://thecounty.me/2026/03/05/news/presque-isle-approves-moratorium-on-new-marijuana-businesses/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The County's Paula Brewer covered the vote</a> and <a href="https://www.wagmtv.com/2026/03/06/presque-isle-votes-halt-marijuana-business-growth/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">WAGM-TV confirmed the unanimous decision</a>. Existing operators (Full Bloom and Royal Leaf, plus the medical-only Caribou store) are unaffected. New entrants to the Presque Isle market will need to wait for the council to lift or modify the pause.
  </Callout>

  <section>
    <h2>Presque Isle's Market Context</h2>
    <p>Presque Isle is the largest city in Aroostook County — and Aroostook is the largest county in the United States east of the Mississippi River, covering 6,672 square miles with only about 67,000 residents. That ratio of land to people defines the cannabis market: dispensaries here serve customers driving an hour or more from towns like Madawaska, Van Buren, or the St. John Valley.</p>
    <p>The University of Maine at Presque Isle adds a small but reliable student base, and the Northern Maine Medical Center and the County healthcare network generate a steady stream of medical cardholders. Two storefront dispensaries on Main Street — one adult-use/recreational (Full Bloom) and one adult-use-only apothecary (Royal Leaf), plus Richardson Remedies ten miles south in Caribou (medical-only) — represent a more developed market than the population density would suggest. It's a function of Aroostook's vast catchment area, plus the fact that the council's March 2026 moratorium is a calibration move rather than a reversal of the existing retail framework.</p>
    <p>Operators evaluating Aroostook should treat Presque Isle as the regional anchor, with Houlton (60 mi south on I-95, medical-only) and Calais (150 mi east on US-1) as secondary nodes. The March 2026 moratorium is a pause on new entrants — not a retreat from the existing two-store Presque Isle market.</p>
  </section>

  
